&lt;h2&gt;About impact.com&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; is the world’s leading commerce partnership marketing platform, transforming the way businesses grow by enabling them to discover, manage, and scale partnerships across the entire customer journey. From affiliates and influencers to content publishers, brand ambassadors, and customer advocates, &lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; empowers brands to drive trusted, performance-based growth through authentic relationships. Its award-winning products—&lt;strong&gt;Performance&lt;/strong&gt; (affiliate), &lt;strong&gt;Creator&lt;/strong&gt; (influencer), and &lt;strong&gt;Advocate&lt;/strong&gt; (customer referral)—unify every type of partner into one integrated platform. As consumers increasingly rely on recommendations from people and communities they trust, &lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; helps brands show up where it matters most. Today, over 5,000 global brands, including Walmart, Uber, Shopify, Lenovo, L’Oréal, and Fanatics, rely on &lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; to power more than 225,000 partnerships that deliver measurable business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Impact&#39;s Data Platform Engineering team is looking for an Associate Data Platform Engineer ready to build real distributed systems skills on large-scale production data. Our platform powers analytics, ML, and data products at TB–PB scale using Scala, Python, Spark, Kafka, Airflow, and BigQuery on GCP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a foundational role for someone early in their career who wants to learn how serious data infrastructure is built and operated, with mentorship from experienced engineers and clear patterns to follow. You&#39;ll work within the Data Analytics Group (DAG) alongside Analytics Engineers, Data Analysts, and Data Scientists, though you won&#39;t own dbt models, metric definitions, or reporting. Our ideal candidate has strong programming and SQL fundamentals, genuine curiosity about how systems behave under load, and good judgement about when to ask for help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role reports to the Team Lead, Data Platform Engineering, and is based in Cape Town, hybrid, with two days per week in office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The platform:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The platform has strong foundations: Scala and Spark pipelines processing TB-scale data, dozens of managed data connectors, Airflow on Astronomer for orchestration, a mature dbt transformation layer, and BigQuery as the core analytical warehouse. You&#39;ll also have room to shape the platform&#39;s next chapter: modernising parts of the compute stack, and building out governance frameworks, data contracts, SLOs, observability, cost management, and data quality monitoring within your domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline development:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and extend batch and streaming pipeline components under guidance. Write clean, tested Scala and Python code. Add Spark transformation steps, build Airflow DAGs, and implement Kafka consumers with senior support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform configuration:&lt;/strong&gt; Configure platform components such as BigQuery tables, partitioning strategies, and Cloud Storage buckets with guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability &amp;amp; data quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Build monitoring dashboards and alerting for job success, latency, and pipeline health. Implement data quality checks to catch anomalies, schema violations, and missing data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations &amp;amp; incident response:&lt;/strong&gt; Shadow the on-call rotation, help investigate root causes, debug using logs, metrics, and traces, and maintain runbooks and operational documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security, governance &amp;amp; cost awareness:&lt;/strong&gt; Follow least-privilege access, secrets management, and PII handling by default. Consider the cost and performance implications of your changes with guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; craft:&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI coding assistants while holding the same quality and review standards. Participate in code reviews, pairing, and technical discussions, and communicate progress and blockers clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3 years of experience in software engineering, data engineering, or a related technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working programming ability in Scala, Java, or Python, with an appetite to become strong in both Scala and Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid SQL fundamentals: joins, aggregations, window functions, and an understanding of query behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of data structures, algorithms, and software engineering basics, including Git and collaborative development workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to or eagerness to learn distributed processing (Spark), streaming (Kafka or Pub/Sub), orchestration (Airflow), and a major cloud platform, ideally GCP (BigQuery, Dataproc, Cloud Storage)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving instincts and a methodical approach to debugging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, suited to an async-first distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to participate in on-call learning and operational work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have (Advantageous) Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internship, academic, or personal project experience building data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to CI/CD, automated testing, or infrastructure as code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data formats such as Parquet, Avro, or JSON&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to dbt, Looker, or BI tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or a related field is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the digital marketing technology industry is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At impact.com, we believe that when you’re happy and fulfilled, you do your best work. That’s why we’ve built a benefits package that supports your well-being, growth, and work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Working: &lt;/strong&gt;Our&lt;strong&gt; Responsible PTO policy&lt;/strong&gt; means you can take the time off you need to rest and recharge. We&#39;re committed to a positive work-life balance and provide a flexible environment that allows you to be happy and fulfilled in both your career and your personal life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Your well-being is a priority. Our mental health and wellness benefit includes up to&lt;strong&gt; 12 fully covered therapy/coaching sessions per year&lt;/strong&gt;, with additional dependent coverage. We also offer a &lt;strong&gt;monthly gym reimbursement&lt;/strong&gt; policy to support your physical health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Stake in Our Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer Restricted Stock Units (RSUs) as part of our total compensation, giving you a stake in the company&#39;s growth with a 3-year vesting schedule, pending Board approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investing in Your Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We’re committed to your continuous learning. Take advantage of our free Coursera subscription and our PXA courses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parental Support: &lt;/strong&gt;We offer a generous parental leave policy, 26 weeks of fully paid leave for the primary caregiver and 13 weeks fully paid leave for the secondary caregiver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Financial Support: We provide a technology stipend to help you set up your home office and a monthly allowance to cover your internet expenses&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;impact.com is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;All employees and applicants for employment shall be given fair treatment and equal employment opportunity regardless of their race, ethnicity or ancestry, color or caste, religion or belief, age, sex (including gender identity, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, pregnancy/maternity), national origin, weight, neurodivergence, disability, marital and civil partnership status, caregiving status, veteran status, genetic information, political affiliation, or other prohibited non-merit factors.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-CT1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at impact.com:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Manager, Finance Systems &amp;amp; Data Governance is responsible for leading the team that governs the integrity, accuracy, and flow of critical business data across all financial systems. This role extends beyond sales contract administration to oversee broader systems data alignment—including CRM data, Contract Lifecycle Management (CLM), billing engines, ERP platforms (such as Salesforce and NetSuite) and in-house platforms (i.e. Operator).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior Manager, Finance Operations and Data, this leader will establish robust validation procedures, resolve data discrepancies between systems, and ensure that upstream operational inputs result in seamless downstream billing, accounting, and financial reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a detail-oriented, systems-savvy supervisor capable of managing a high-performing data team, driving automation in data verification, and acting as a bridge between Sales Operations and Finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Development: Lead, mentor, and manage daily operations of the Finance Data Operations team, ensuring appropriate resource allocation, productivity, and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System &amp;amp; Data Alignment: Oversee and reconcile data interfaces and data flows between front-end systems (Salesforce), Contract Lifecycle Management (CLM) tools, billing/financial engines (NetSuite) and in-house platforms/data warehouses (eg. Operator and BigQuery) to guarantee system-to-system consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validation &amp;amp; Quality Control: Implement rigorous validation protocols for critical sales, billing, and pricing data to ensure complete accuracy before billing cycles or downstream accounting closures occur (or any other function relying on the data).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contract &amp;amp; Revenue Integrity: Manage contract administration processes, verifying that finalized sales agreements match financial schedules, pricing models, and compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner directly with Sales Operations, Billings, Revenue, and Accounting teams to troubleshoot system integration issues and optimize upstream data capture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Variable Compensation Support: Ensure timely validation and preparation of sales data, system performance metrics, and reporting necessary for variable compensation calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Improvement &amp;amp; Automation: Identify opportunities to automate manual data validation processes, implement best practices, and document Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit &amp;amp; Compliance Management: Lead the preparation of internal and external data audit requests, ensuring meticulous record-keeping and data preservation standards are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on player-coach who actively participates in daily processes to ensure data accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of working as player-coach in a finance systems &amp;amp; data governance, finance data operations, sales operations or system reconciliation role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a global or multinational B2B environment is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Business Acumen:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid leadership or supervisory experience of 4 or more direct reports with a specific focus on finance systems &amp;amp; data governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to digest, synthesize, and resolve complex systemic errors under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;demonstrating the ability to foster teamwork and support direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate at both operational and managerial levels of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree / Qualifications:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tertiary level qualification in Information Systems, Commerce, Business Administration, Accounting, or a related analytical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance &amp;amp; Data Governance:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous attention to detail and high standard of data hygiene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust understanding of financial processes, specifically Sales Ordering, Revenue Recognition, and Billings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong capabilities in designing, optimizing, and maintaining data flows and validation routines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems &amp;amp; Tools:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on experience with Salesforce (CRM) and/or formal Contract Lifecycle Management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working with NetSuite or similar mid-market/enterprise ERP platforms is highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of advanced Excel, Google Sheets, or data reconciliation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in automation and AI tools to ensure efficiencies in validation and reconciliations of data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with using data warehouses and tools such as BigQuery to manipulate and understand/extract large sets of data in daily operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid, Casual work environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible PTO policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take the time off that you need. We are truly committed to a positive work-life balance, recognising that it is important to be happy and fulfilled in both&lt;/li&gt;
