&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Company:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At impact.com we are passionate about our people, our technology, and are obsessed with customer success. Working together enables us to grow rapidly, win, and serve the largest brands in the world. We use cutting edge technology to solve real-world problems for our clients and continue to pull ahead of the pack as the leading SaaS platform for businesses to automate their partnerships and grow their revenue like never before. We have an entrepreneurial spirit and a culture where ambition and curiosity is rewarded. If you are looking to join a team where your opinion is valued, your contributions are noticed, and enjoy working with fun and talented people from all over the world, then this is the place for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;impact.com, the world’s leading partnership management platform, is transforming the way businesses manage and optimize all types of partnerships—including traditional rewards affiliates, influencers, commerce content publishers, B2B, and more. The company’s powerful, purpose-built platform makes it easy for businesses to create, manage, and scale an ecosystem of partnerships with the brands and communities that customers trust to make purchases, get information, and entertain themselves at home, at work, or on the go. To learn more about how impact.com’s technology platform and partnerships marketplace is driving revenue growth for global enterprise brands such as Walmart, Uber, Shopify, Lenovo, L’Oreal, and Fanatics, visit&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.impact.com&quot;&gt; www.impact.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Creator Solutions team, impact.com’s in-house performance creator experts, you will be responsible for driving success across a portfolio of client accounts. You will manage creator programs and campaigns across diverse verticals, including fashion, parenting, food, technology, and more. Our programs span from introductory performance-led strategies to year-long brand ambassador initiatives. In this role, you will own the campaign execution cycle from start to finish for a select group of clients while providing key support on a variety of larger, strategic programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;impact.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the primary driver of growth and engagement within our clients&#39; Creator and Affiliate Programs. This involves partnering with our brands to design, implement, and scale comprehensive strategies for creator recruitment, relationship management, and community growth, ensuring a vibrant, active, and profitable partner network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement performance-led strategies to attract creators aligned with defined brand and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategize content creation and casting to ensure campaigns are on trend and highly relevant to the current social media landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Campaign Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a 360° creator recruitment effort, identifying and targeting creators to join programs/campaigns, leveraging offshore support where necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source and vet qualified creators for each campaign, providing data-driven recommendations based on follower count, location, niche, and audience demographics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create comprehensive creator campaign briefs based on client guidelines and FTC/disclosure compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client &amp;amp; Creator Management&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads&amp;nbsp; kick-off calls and prepare all necessary documentation (internal and external), efficiently responding to client communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate terms and communicate extensively with creators, including facilitating product orders and gathering content drafts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve creator content to ensure compliance with the brief and quality standards (e.g., spelling and grammar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide excellent customer service and subject matter expertise, ensuring client and creator satisfaction and trust in our services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage program timelines and budgets to ensure both revenue goals and client deadlines are consistently met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather campaign metrics, analyze performance, and format data to generate actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential upselling opportunities and communicate these effectively to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute incentive programs, including flat fees, performance-based rewards, and exclusive offers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with internal teams (community support, sales, product, marketing, and client success) to ensure creator community and affiliate strategies align with overarching business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adventageous: Completion of your free &lt;a href=&quot;https://pxa.impact.com/student/path/1099689-getting-started-with-influencer-partnerships-learning-path-certification?utm_source=impact.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=featured-link&amp;amp;utm_content=asso-lp-220&amp;amp;utm_campaign=job-description&quot;&gt;Getting Started with Influencer Partnerships Certification&lt;/a&gt; on PXA. &lt;em&gt;Candidates must mention this completion in their cover letter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree or relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2-4+ years of proven professional experience in the Affiliate Marketing, Creator Marketing, or Community Management space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundational knowledge of creator and affiliate marketing strategies, tools, and technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the impact.com or another affiliate marketing platform is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of creators across verticals, especially CPG, fashion, parenting, wellness, fitness, etc., and creator rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with niches such as gaming, tech, finance, entertainment, etc. a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the essential components of the creator lifecycle: budgeting, casting, negotiating, contracting, fulfillment oversight, draft approvals, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills (written and verbal) with demonstrated ability to engage and motivate diverse Creators, affiliates, and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven mindset with proficiency in analyzing metrics and translating them into actionable business insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship-driven approach with the ability to manage diverse personalities and work styles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong passion for and knowledge of social media platforms and the ability to adapt to sudden changes in trends and industry shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mentality with a strong drive to develop client businesses and succeed personally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities, and thrive in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a growth mindset and a willingness to continuously learn and improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At impact.com, we believe that when you’re happy and fulfilled, you do your best work. That’s why we’ve built a benefits package that supports your well-being, growth, and work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Working:&lt;/strong&gt; Our Responsible PTO policy means you can take the time off you need to rest and recharge. We&#39;re committed to a positive work-life balance and provide a flexible environment that allows you to be happy and fulfilled in both your career and your personal life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health and Wellness:&lt;/strong&gt; Your well-being is a priority. Our mental health and wellness benefit includes up to 12 fully covered therapy/coaching sessions per year, with additional dependent coverage. We also offer a monthly gym reimbursement policy to support your physical health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investing in Your Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We’re committed to your continuous learning. Take advantage of our free Coursera subscription and our PXA courses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parental Support:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer a generous parental leave policy, 26 weeks of fully paid leave for the primary caregiver and 13 weeks fully paid leave for the secondary caregiver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Financial Support:&lt;/strong&gt; We provide a technology stipend to help you set up your home office and a monthly allowance to cover your internet expenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Company:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; is the world’s leading commerce partnership marketing platform, transforming the way businesses grow by enabling them to discover, manage, and scale partnerships across the entire customer journey. From affiliates and influencers to content publishers, brand ambassadors, and customer advocates, &lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; empowers brands to drive trusted, performance-based growth through authentic relationships. Its award-winning products &lt;strong&gt;Performance&lt;/strong&gt; (affiliate), &lt;strong&gt;Creator&lt;/strong&gt; (influencer), and &lt;strong&gt;Advocate&lt;/strong&gt; (customer referral) unify every type of partner into one integrated platform. As consumers increasingly rely on recommendations from people and communities they trust,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; helps brands show up where it matters most. Today, over 5,000 global brands, including Walmart, Uber, Shopify, Lenovo, L’Oréal, and Fanatics, rely on &lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com/&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; to power more than 225,000 partnerships that deliver measurable business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at impact.com:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member of the Creator Solutions team, our internal creator marketing experts, you will support the successful management of multiple accounts spanning diverse verticals, such as fashion, parenting, food, and technology. The team&#39;s mission is to execute and scale our brands&#39; Creator Communities. You will learn how we drive partner recruitment, strategic engagement, and growth to cultivate a vibrant and high-performing partner network, contributing directly to campaigns from brief development to long-term ambassador programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Creator Solutions Intern will be integral to campaign success and will be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Campaign Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Assisting with campaign execution, from initial creator casting through to final performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Management &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Joining client kick-off calls, meticulously documenting action items and recap notes, and providing proactive client support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creator Relationship Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicating directly with creators, including negotiating payments and campaign terms to foster ongoing relationships, in partnership with Senior Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure both clients and creators receive exceptional customer service and expert guidance that enhances our excellent service offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Casting: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with multiple clients in various verticals to help grow their programs through a curated selection of partner recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Marketing, Communications, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of experience contributing to creator marketing, digital marketing, or performance marketing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of the creator lifecycle, including casting, budgeting, negotiation, contracting, content fulfillment oversight, and reporting creator verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous agency experience or demonstrated knowledge of creator rates is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication, organization, and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a growth mindset and a willingness to continuously learn and improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven problem-solving capabilities and the ability to thrive under tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic proficiency in Google Sheets &amp;amp; Excel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advantageous: Completion of your free&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://pxa.impact.com/student/path/1099689-getting-started-with-influencer-partnerships-learning-path-certification?utm_source=impact.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=featured-link&amp;amp;utm_content=asso-lp-220&amp;amp;utm_campaign=job-description&quot;&gt;Getting Started with Influencer Partnerships Certification&lt;/a&gt; on PXA. &lt;em&gt;Candidates must mention this completion in their cover letter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a six month hybrid internship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits/Perks for interns:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Casual work environment, including working from home&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible work hours&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training &amp;amp; Development&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Learning the advanced partnership automation products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Coursera&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internet Allowance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Free &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://pxa.impact.com/student/path/1099626-affiliate-partnerships-industry-fundamentals-certification-path?utm_source=impact.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=featured-link&amp;amp;utm_content=fund-lp-100&amp;amp;utm_campaign=job-description&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Affiliate &amp;amp; Partnerships Industry Fundamentals Certification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; by PXA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Impact is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, colour, ethnicity, religion, creed, national origin, ancestry, genetics, sex, pregnancy or childbirth, sexual orientation, gender (including gender identity or non-binary or nonconformity and/or status as a trans individual), age, physical or mental disability, citizenship, marital, parental and/or familial status, past, current or prospective service in the uniformed services, or any characteristic protected under applicable law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-ND1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About impact.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;impact.com is the world’s leading commerce partnership marketing platform, transforming the way businesses grow by enabling them to discover, manage, and scale partnerships across the entire customer journey. From affiliates and influencers to content publishers, brand ambassadors, and customer advocates, impact.com empowers brands to drive trusted, performance-based growth through authentic relationships. Its award-winning products - Performance (affiliate), Creator (influencer), and Advocate (customer referral) - unify every type of partner into one integrated platform. As consumers increasingly rely on recommendations from people and communities they trust, impact.com helps brands show up where it matters most. Today, over 5,000 global brands - including Walmart, Uber, Shopify, Lenovo, L’Oréal, and Fanatics - rely on &lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fimpact.com&amp;amp;esheet=54399906&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260120914149&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=impact.com&amp;amp;index=38&amp;amp;md5=c467739484a5a8610aff0747572ac8cb&quot;&gt;impact.com&lt;/a&gt; to power more than 350,000 partnerships that deliver measurable business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at impact.com:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world’s largest advertisers are rebuilding their creator programs around performance. They no longer want campaigns alone — they want an always-on operating system: a center of excellence with the strategy, compensation model, a scaled casting engine, a new measurement framework, and the internal muscle to run it at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;That is what you build.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Creator Solutions Account Manager, you are a member of impact.com’s Creator Strategy practice, designing and optimizing the most performance creator programs in the market. You work directly with brand teams and their agencies — diagnosing what they actually need beneath what they’ve asked for, translating ambiguity into roadmaps, and then standing up in front of a room and teaching others how to run it. You are equal parts strategist, executer, architect, creative, innovator, facilitator, and teacher.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a client-facing, high-visibility role for someone who thrives in fast moving environments with demanding stakeholders, and wants to help define what performance creator marketing becomes over the next five years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a working point of view on social and performance media trends, and pressure-test which ones deserve client investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage the client relationship across a portfolio of accounts, from strategy and planning through to launch, optimisation, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse campaign performance and manage reporting, translating data into clear insights and strategic recommendations to optimise programs and support client growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build creative strategies that focus on affiliate-optimized formats, translating what converts on performance rails into briefs creators can actually execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a working point of view on social and performance media trends, and pressure-test which ones deserve client investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop breakthrough data-driven creator strategies, including campaign proposals, pricing recommendations, budget allocation, creator selection, and content formats that drive measurable performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with clients as a trusted advisor, translating performance data into actionable insights, optimisation plans, and opportunities for program growth and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively cultivate client relationships by building trust both within and outside of work settings, including hosting client strategy meetings, dinners, and activities that strengthen long-term partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert on impact.com and assist top clients with best practices and strategies utilizing the platform. This includes building strong relationships with Customer Success team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Customer Success, Marketing, and Community teams to align creator strategies with broader business goals, while managing budgets and timelines effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Supervision &amp;amp; Client Handoff: Supervise Sr Associates and Leads activities, ensuring consistent operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of your free &lt;a href=&quot;https://pxa.impact.com/student/path/1099689-getting-started-with-influencer-partnerships-learning-path-certification?utm_source=impact.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=featured-link&amp;amp;utm_content=asso-lp-220&amp;amp;utm_campaign=job-description&quot;&gt;Getting Started with Influencer Partnerships Certification&lt;/a&gt; on PXA is advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience leading integrated strategy and execution within creator marketing, affiliate marketing, paid media, or community-led programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in a client-facing, consultative role, with confidence shaping complete strategy decks, influencing decisions, and driving account growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven mindset, with the ability to analyse performance metrics and turn insights into clear recommendations and scalable strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the creator ecosystem across major social platforms, trends, and verticals such as fashion, CPG, parenting, wellness, or tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and pitching strategic proposals and campaign plans to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrated media experience with paid media, social media, and affiliate marketing delivers a holistic strategy to creator programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with different measurement methods and models such as attribution, marketing mix modeling, brand health tracking, and lift studies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, organised, and solutions-focused approach, comfortable managing multiple campaigns in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage creators, talent managers, and senior clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of the Getting Started with Influencer Partnerships Certification on PXA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable being handed a vague directive and returning with a clear roadmap, requirements, and stakeholder alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge across performance marketing, affiliate marketing, and creator marketing, and fluency in the SaaS platforms that power them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency with leading performance creator platforms such as LTK and ShopMy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level public speaking. You can hold a room of senior marketers and make a complicated idea land.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level workshop design and facilitation — you know the difference between presenting and facilitating, and you’re good at both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in advanced marketing measurement: MMM, brand lift, sales lift, MTA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management discipline across multiple concurrent, high-stakes engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A process optimizer’s instinct — you notice friction and fix it rather than routing around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine appetite for teaching. The best outcome of your work is a client team that no longer needs you in the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thought leadership: you’re not just applying performance creator marketing best practice, you’re inventing it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in measurement technology and the vendor landscape behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with performance paid media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published writing, speaking, or original research in the creator or performance marketing space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
