&lt;h4&gt;**Must be located in NYC or Santa Barbara, California**&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Company:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At impact.com our culture is our soul. We are passionate about our people, our technology, and are obsessed with customer success. Working together enables us to grow rapidly, win, and serve the largest brands in the world. We use cutting edge technology to solve real-world problems for our clients and continue to pull ahead of the pack as the leading SaaS platform for businesses to automate their partnerships and grow their revenue like never before. We have an entrepreneurial spirit and a culture where ambition and curiosity is rewarded. If you are looking to join a team where your opinion is valued, your contributions are noticed, and enjoy working with fun and talented people from all over the world, then this is the place for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;impact.com, the world&#39;s leading partnership management platform, is transforming the way businesses manage and optimize all types of partnerships-including traditional rewards affiliates, influencers, commerce content publishers, B2B, and more. The company&#39;s powerful, purpose-built platform makes it easy for businesses to create, manage, and scale an ecosystem of partnerships with the brands and communities that customers trust to make purchases, get information, and entertain themselves at home, at work, or on the go. To learn more about how impact.com&#39;s technology platform and partnerships marketplace is driving revenue growth for global enterprise brands such as Walmart, Uber, Shopify, Lenovo, Fanatics, visit www.impact.com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role is exciting!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;We are looking for a sales leader who believes great teams are built through high standards, disciplined execution, and relentless people development. As RVP of SMB, you will lead a team of SMB Account Executives who own territories of small and medium-sized brands and run a high volume of deals from first call to signed contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;This role is for someone who loves coaching, owns both the pipeline and the number, and sees recruiting and pipeline creation as core leadership responsibilities. The strongest sellers you develop will move up market to Mid-Market and Enterprise or into leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the standard&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Lead with elite expectations for performance, preparation, and professionalism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Build a culture of accountability where commitments matter and results are inspected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Balance high standards with deep investment in each AE&#39;s growth, and create urgency without panic so the team stays confident the number is reachable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and develop a world-class team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Own recruiting end to end: source candidates yourself every week, assess for coachability, resilience, integrity, and growth mindset, and keep raising the hiring bar with every AE you hire&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Coach reps in the moment on live deals, and build the SMB fundamentals over time: tying each request to a real business priority, confirming who owns the budget and the path to signature, turning interest into firm next steps, and building a business case in plain dollars from the customer&#39;s own numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Run rigorous weekly one-on-ones that blend deal inspection, skill development, and career growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Build an individual coaching plan for each AE, coach top and bottom performers differently, and track skill lift and performance improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Ramp new hires on a clear path, and promote your strongest sellers to Mid-Market, Enterprise, or leadership once their results and deal work show they are ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own pipeline and revenue outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Own pipeline creation standards, leading indicators, and coverage ratios. Set each AE&#39;s monthly pipeline goal from their quota and inspect progress against it every week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Make each AE the owner of their territory and their pipeline. Most pipeline should come from AE-sourced outbound, with inbound and SDR leads treated as extra, not the plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Run a weekly operating cadence built on leading indicators: AE-sourced meetings set and held, meeting-to-opportunity conversion, territory penetration, and outbound effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Find why each rep is short on pipeline, whether activity, targeting, messaging, or conversion, and coach the biggest gap first so the team gets more effective, not just busier&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Make sure every AE prioritizes the right accounts in their territory and works their highest-value accounts hard enough.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Inspect deals honestly and coach reps to keep deals moving fast without skipping discovery or qualification: discovery before demo, MEDDPICC, clear next steps, and value over discounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Maintain high forecast integrity through disciplined inspection and data-driven judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Does this sound like you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;2+ years managing quota-carrying Account Executives in SaaS, ideally in a high-velocity SMB sales motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;A strong track record as a new-business individual closer, including self-sourcing your own pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;A track record of overachievement against individual and team quotas, with team results you can walk through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;A team that built most of its own pipeline under your leadership, with the numbers to show it: coverage, sourcing mix, and conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Examples of reps you coached from underperforming to high-achieving, and AEs you hired who went on to earn promotion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience sourcing, interviewing, and hiring AEs, with a clear view of what separates a strong hire from a strong interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;A clear leadership philosophy and a weekly operating rhythm you can walk us through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Fluency in a sales methodology such as MEDDPICC, Challenger, or Command of the Message, and experience coaching a team to use it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Comfort running a forecast from deal-level evidence and pipeline data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong empathy for peers, direct reports, and customers, and the communication skills to motivate behavior change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience in performance, partner, or affiliate marketing is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Ability to work from our New York City or Santa Barbara office a minimum of 3 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you lead:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coach first.&lt;/strong&gt; You give feedback specific enough to check, and you follow up to see whether it stuck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Selective.&lt;/strong&gt; You hire for coachability over polish, and you would rather keep a seat open than fill it with the wrong person&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious.&lt;/strong&gt; You ask your reps more questions than you answer, and you diagnose a problem before you prescribe a fix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountable.&lt;/strong&gt; You hold your team to its pipeline as firmly as its bookings, and you keep belief high when a month starts slow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range: $260K-320k &lt;/strong&gt;OTE&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;potential&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;total on target earnings &lt;strong&gt;($130K-$160k base + $130K-$160k commission)&lt;/strong&gt;, per year, plus eligibility to receive a Restricted Stock Unit (RSU) grant.&lt;/p&gt;
