&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About impact.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;impact.com is the world’s leading commerce partnership marketing platform, transforming the way businesses grow by enabling them to discover, manage, and scale partnerships across the entire customer journey. From affiliates and influencers to content publishers, brand ambassadors, and customer advocates, impact.com empowers brands to drive trusted, performance-based growth through authentic relationships. Its award-winning products—Performance (affiliate), Creator (influencer), and Advocate (customer referral)—unify every type of partner into one integrated platform. As consumers increasingly rely on recommendations from people and communities they trust, impact.com helps brands show up where it matters most. Today, over 5,000 global brands, including Walmart, Uber, Shopify, Lenovo, L’Oréal, and Fanatics, rely on impact.com to power more than 225,000 partnerships that deliver measurable business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;impact.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we grow across EMEA and beyond, we’re looking for a Senior Global Payroll Specialist&amp;nbsp;based in Cape Town to support the accurate and timely delivery of payroll across several&amp;nbsp;countries. You’ll work closely with People Excellence (HR), Finance, Operations,&amp;nbsp;employees, and payroll vendors to manage the day-to-day and end-to-end payroll&amp;nbsp;processes. This role is ideal for someone who is detail-oriented, organised, responsive,&amp;nbsp;and takes ownership of their work. You’ll support countries such as South Africa, UK,&amp;nbsp;Netherlands, Italy, Germany and Norway, with opportunities to grow your expertise acrossmore regions as we expand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the day-to-day end-to-end payroll process for multiple EMEA countries, ensuring payroll is processed accurately, on time, and in accordance with local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of payroll issues through to resolution and proactively identify opportunities to improve the efficiency, accuracy, and effectiveness of day-to-day payroll processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate payroll records and documentation, following established payroll processes, controls, and confidentiality requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support statutory payroll requirements and submissions, ensuring relevant deadlines are tracked and met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear and responsive payroll support to employees, resolving queries within agreed SLAs and prioritising urgent or time-sensitive matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review payroll reports, payment files, reconciliations, and other payroll documentation required for each payroll cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with payroll vendors to provide accurate inputs, review payroll outputs, follow up on issues, and ensure agreed payroll timelines are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with People Excellence and Finance to ensure payroll data is accurately reflected between the HR system, payroll software, and payroll accounting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform payroll checks, reconciliations, and variance analysis to identify and resolve discrepancies before payroll is finalised.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date on local regulations and labour laws impacting the payroll process, and ensure compliance across all payroll tax jurisdictions in which we operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external auditors on audits, substantive testing, walkthroughs, and all other information gathering related to payroll.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Leverage technology to improve efficiencies within the global payroll team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years of multi-country payroll experience in private and public company environments;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with payroll systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive and positive working attitude, with a willingness to learn, support the team, and look for practical ways to improve processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time-management skills, with a clear sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;around payroll deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of ownership and accountability, with the ability to follow tasks through to completion and escalate issues when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator, both written and verbal; reliable and responsive to email and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slack communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of integrity, discretion, and professionalism when handling confidential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;payroll and employee information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent computer skills, including Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Docs, and Microsoft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Office, including pivot tables, LOOKUPs, conditional formatting, and IF/AND formulas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of the payroll function including preparation, balancing, internal control, and payroll taxes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
